# game_ui_manager.md

**Deprecated:** The **GameUIManager** is the legacy overlay loader and renderer that keeps older HUD elements working while new modular UI systems replace them.

**Note:** All systems are modular and self-contained. See [docs/modular/game_system_tree.md](../../modular/game_system_tree.md) for the latest status. A system remains **In-Progress** until its documentation, cleanup, and tests are merged and verified.

## Layout Loading

`GameHUD::loadLayout(name)` reads the layout description for the requested overlay at runtime. Each entry provides `x` and `y` offsets and an optional `anchor` string. Anchors map to `OverlayAnchor` enums so elements may be positioned relative to the screen corners or center. Missing or malformed entries trigger warnings and fall back to built‑in default positions.

All offsets in the layout file are specified in **Virtual Grid Units** on a 1000×1000 grid. `GameUIManager` forwards these positions directly to the renderer without any scaling by the view size. Anchor calculations and layout coordinates are interpreted purely in VGU space. Utility helpers expect the current view dimensions expressed in VGU so overlays behave consistently at any resolution. The newer `AlignmentHelpers` set – including helpers for each screen corner – offers similar behavior without requiring manual anchor enums.

## Rendering Flow

`RenderUI()` is called once per frame. It checks if the game is over and logs that transition. Each active overlay draws through the renderer's batched primitives, ensuring UI elements share the same rendering pipeline as the rest of the game.
